{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1081457-languages-a-background-or-a-knowledge","id":1081457,"title":"Languages a Background or a Knowledge?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-04-20T09:09:00-07:00","id":1081457,"title":"<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/icons/icon5.png\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" alt=\"\" /> Languages a Background or a Knowledge?","content":"What would languages beyond a PC's native fall under on a character sheet? I thought it was a background, but I didn't see a description for it in the Werewolf book. <br /> <br /> Note, I am talking about human languages such as Spanish, German, American Sign Language. Not supernatural Languages.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-20T09:45:53-07:00","id":1081468,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wonderandawe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1081457-languages-a-background-or-a-knowledge#post1081457\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What would languages beyond a PC's native fall under on a character sheet? I thought it was a background, but I didn't see a description for it in the Werewolf book.<br /> <br /> Note, I am talking about human languages such as Spanish, German, American Sign Language. Not supernatural Languages.</div> </div> </div> </div>Language is a 1 point Mental Merit which can be taken multiple times, each adding an additional known language.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2008-cynic01","name":"Cynic01","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"437"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-20T09:47:57-07:00","id":1081469,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cynic01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1081457-languages-a-background-or-a-knowledge?p=1081468#post1081468\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Language is a 1 point Mental Merit which can be taken multiple times, each adding an additional known language.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Do you know what book I can find the merit description in?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-20T09:59:16-07:00","id":1081473,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wonderandawe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1081457-languages-a-background-or-a-knowledge?p=1081469#post1081469\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Do you know what book I can find the merit description in?</div> </div> </div> </div>W20 and V20","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2008-cynic01","name":"Cynic01","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"437"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-20T10:03:23-07:00","id":1081475,"title":"","content":"Doh! I've been looking in the wrong spot. <br /> <br /> Thanks for your help. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-20T10:11:15-07:00","id":1081478,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cynic01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1081457-languages-a-background-or-a-knowledge?p=1081473#post1081473\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> W20 and V20</div> </div> </div> </div>Also M20, and probably all future 20th anniversary editions, too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-20T10:42:07-07:00","id":1081491,"title":"","content":"Making most europeans have to pay merits for languages is the best argument I have ever seen for not having a cap on merits.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11581-patricthomas","name":"PatricThomas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-20T11:55:37-07:00","id":1081518,"title":"","content":"The majority of the cores books don't have a cap on Merits, just a suggested 7 point cap on Flaws. People putting caps on Merits are generally making a house rule, not using the RAW (within reason, the limits on Merits and Flaws is RAW flexible to the ST's judgemental calls).<br /> <br /> There's also the Natural Linguist Merit which makes characters that speak more than four languages much cheaper to do (and gets you additional benefits which could be applied to translating languages you don't know but should have a chance to decipher).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-20T12:09:01-07:00","id":1081527,"title":"","content":"Natural Linguist doubles the number of languages you get per point of Merit, which means you get four language for four freebie points and then two language per freebie point beyond that (and let us not forget that it gives you three dice on any dice pool dealing with written or spoken languages). I generally restrict the dice pool bonus to only using the Expression Talent, but it is still one of those Merits that everyone should purchase (+3 dice for 2 freebie points on every use of a particular Ability is something that no one should ignore).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-20T15:33:45-07:00","id":1081604,"title":"","content":"Language as a merit is just bad mechanic in my opinion, being able to speak a second language is not as advantageous as 1 point in ressource or a ghoul or most other background/1pt merit.<br /> <br /> In most games, it probably either won't come into play or be so mandatory that it would be a merit tax for all players.<br /> <br /> It's better to agree at chargen the modern language spoken by the character depending on it's backgrounds, in agreement with the ST, as for old language like Latin, same but also dependents on dots in Academic.<br /> <br /> The only interest for Natural Linguist would be (still in my opinion) on a quite historically accurate DA campaign in a place where you'd be regularly meeting people speaking different language/dialects.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5462-kendaan","name":"Kendaan","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"150"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-20T16:32:34-07:00","id":1081619,"title":"","content":"The usefulness of languages is one of those super-subjective things, which is why it's actually best as a Merit instead of the old placement in the Linguistics Knowledge.<br /> <br /> I also highly disagree with the idea that languages are a binary thing where either you never need it (but then you never have to take a Merit), or every player is going to take the Merit.<br /> <br /> I've been in plenty of games where only a few characters heavily invest in Languages, and it's always been useful for them to do so. The most common setup I see is the &quot;face&quot; character that speaks all of the common modern languages, and as the best social character is doing a lot of the talking with NPCs anyway, spoken in the setting of the game, and the &quot;academic&quot; character that has a good smattering of ancient languages to get in the occult investigation stuff. Both character archetypes get value for the investment, and can do enough that there isn't a need for everyone to get it.<br /> <br /> Of course, it's situational. In Mage games, the Language Merit is exceedingly common to the point of mandatory because so many groups use language as part of their Instruments, but there's lots of ways to avoid it if you need to. A Chorister doesn't need to be fluent in a language that they pray in to use it for magic.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-20T16:47:45-07:00","id":1081628,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1081457-languages-a-background-or-a-knowledge?p=1081619#post1081619\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've been in plenty of games where only a few characters heavily invest in Languages, and it's always been useful for them to do so.</div> </div> </div> </div>But did it got into play because the player had the merit &amp;the ST wanted to make it useful or if no player had taken it they would have been unable to interact with these NPC?<br /> <br /> Although I do agree, it's better than when it was a knowledge.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5462,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5462-kendaan","user":"Kendaan","date":". 04-20-2017, 07:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5462-kendaan","name":"Kendaan","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"150"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-20T21:25:18-07:00","id":1081699,"title":"","content":"Given the nature of any point-buy game, part of GMing is adapting the setting/etc. of the thing you're running to what the players make. If nobody makes a combat capable PC, you don't throw lots of combat heavy stuff at them. If you do have a combat heavy PC, you include combat because that lets that player have fun.<br /> <br /> So to me, the question is sort of a chicken or egg sort of thing. Unless your ST is very set on a specific story path you follow and you have to get past the NPC that only speaks language X by talking to them without any ability to get help, it matters as much as the group makes it matter... which is true of anything in the game.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-20T21:35:12-07:00","id":1081703,"title":"","content":"It is not the bonus languages that make Natural Linguist such a good Merit, it is the +3 dice bonus to Expression. You are paying two freebie points for six freebie points worth of benefit (plus the bonus languages).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-21T00:29:25-07:00","id":1081739,"title":"","content":"This is one of those times I throw out the rules and let players just take languages, if it makes sense for thier character. Anything more than a passing, casual conversational ability gets folded into Academics, and dead languages (or even Ecclesiastical Latin) falls under Academics at my table. <br /> <br /> Cheers!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If you don't use an Oxford comma, I feel bad for you, son,<br /> 'Cuz I got ninety-nine problems, but clarity ain't one.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/408-nothing","name":"nothing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar408_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"572"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-21T15:35:01-07:00","id":1082031,"title":"","content":"I like the exponential growth method because spending 1 point to represent being mildly bilingual makes sense to me but there's a drop off rate for how useful an extra language will be after the first plus its easier to learn.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-21T16:18:31-07:00","id":1082046,"title":"","content":"The problem is that the exponential growth method with Linguistics is only beneficial at character creation (when it is bought with linear points). With XP, the costs are also geometric, making it largely not a real difference.<br /> <br /> I also don't buy any claim that learning one language makes learning new languages easier. Even for closely related languages, this can trip people up because the similarities make it harder to remember the key differences.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-21T17:31:24-07:00","id":1082069,"title":"","content":"The record is around 60 languages, so the Merit system of languages at least approaches that level (a maximum of 41 languages, including native language, is possible at character creation, though anything beyond 11 languages is probably silly).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-21T18:00:25-07:00","id":1082076,"title":"","content":"For what its worth our group has recently house ruled that 1 additional language is learned at Academics 1, 3 and 5 for free. The basis being that to graduate from high school on a college prep curriculum you need to take a foreign language, which is more or less the 1st dot of Academics. Then 4 and 6/8 year degrees are affording you others. For deciphering written languages we use Enigmas which of course could have a Language specialty if desired. For additional languages we use the Merit. <br /> <br /> It works out great and players don't feel like they are wasting points on something they rarely use more than once or twice in a chronicle.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/987-tuch","name":"Tuch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar987_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-21T18:04:58-07:00","id":1082079,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1081457-languages-a-background-or-a-knowledge?p=1082046#post1082046\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I also don't buy any claim that learning one language makes learning new languages easier. Even for closely related languages, this can trip people up because the similarities make it harder to remember the key differences.</div> </div> </div> </div>It is known to be the case experimentally that third language acquisition is faster than second. The &quot;speed up&quot; is mostly &quot;language distance&quot; invariant, although languages closer to one's own are always easier absolutely. The effect plateaus at some point (fifth language in most studies)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3326-an-fhuiseog","name":"An Fhuiseog","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3326_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"271"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-21T19:39:40-07:00","id":1082098,"title":"","content":"As far as I'm aware those studies are focused on early language education (as in children) where being raised in a multilingual fashion helps later language acquisition. And &quot;faster&quot; is not the same as, &quot;easier.&quot;<br /> <br /> And no, closer languages are not always easier absolutely. My father and sister share language related learning disabilities that made it easier for them to learn distant languages than close ones.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-21T22:26:19-07:00","id":1082154,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1081457-languages-a-background-or-a-knowledge?p=1082098#post1082098\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As far as I'm aware those studies are focused on early language education (as in children) where being raised in a multilingual fashion helps later language acquisition. And &quot;faster&quot; is not the same as, &quot;easier.&quot;<br /> <br /> And no, closer languages are not always easier absolutely. My father and sister share language related learning disabilities that made it easier for them to learn distant languages than close ones.</div> </div> </div> </div>the Keyword there is disability.<br /> <br /> And my second point was there is a distinct drop off in usefulness for a character, its alot easier for an st to make knowing 2 languages matter in plot vs 50. So I'm willing to accept learning extra languages is &quot;easier&quot; or at least close enough for the not even close to realism mechanics of the setting and that gamewise knowing 50 languages is more a character quirk than a setting revolver.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-22T02:18:33-07:00","id":1082194,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1081457-languages-a-background-or-a-knowledge?p=1082154#post1082154\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">the Keyword there is disability.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, it isn't. The key word is &quot;absolutely,&quot; because that is saying that something is 100% true in all cases is incorrect if presented with contrary evidence; even if considered outliers.<br /> <br /> As well, we only call them learning disabilities because it slots them into legislation to protect the education of children with disabilities to ensure appropriate steps are taken. All a learning disability is, is when &quot;normal&quot; teaching methods don't work for a student severely enough that a certified professional signs off of them needing alternate methods of instruction.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And my second point was there is a distinct drop off in usefulness for a character, its alot easier for an st to make knowing 2 languages matter in plot vs 50. So I'm willing to accept learning extra languages is &quot;easier&quot; or at least close enough for the not even close to realism mechanics of the setting and that gamewise knowing 50 languages is more a character quirk than a setting revolver. </div> </div> </div>This doesn't make any sense as a defense of the geometric Linguistics Knowledge model of pre-20th.<br /> <br /> An Ability dot is worth 2 freebies. The value of Linguistics doesn't get cheaper than the Language Merit until Linguistics 5 (at which point you're dealing with 16 languages, and are certainly in the point of making it hard to make them all matter to the plot). The &quot;linear&quot; Merit approach is better because individual languages are cheap until you get into the very high numbers of them. You can get the 1-2 extra languages that you feel are worth taking for player for less investment than using the old version.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-22T02:38:02-07:00","id":1082198,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1081457-languages-a-background-or-a-knowledge?p=1082098#post1082098\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As far as I'm aware those studies are focused on early language education (as in children) where being raised in a multilingual fashion helps later language acquisition. And &quot;faster&quot; is not the same as, &quot;easier.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>No there are studies with adults as well, I can give you references if you want. The entire learning process is enhanced, vocabulary retention, rate of syntax acquisition, everything that one would colloquially summarise as &quot;easier&quot;.<br /> <br /> I meant absolutely in the sense of &quot;ignoring the relative&quot;, rather than &quot; absolute&quot; as in &quot;always true&quot;. Better expressed, the speed up in third language acquisition will not cause more distant languages to become easier than those in the same family.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And no, closer languages are not always easier absolutely. My father and sister share language related learning disabilities that made it easier for them to learn distant languages than close ones. </div> </div> </div>All major meta-studies demonstrate that languages with a historical or syntactic relationship to ones own are acquired faster. I've never read an account of such a disability, how does it affect their acquisition of closer languages vs further ones? What do you mean by closer, other Indo-European languages?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3326,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3326-an-fhuiseog","user":"An Fhuiseog","date":". 04-22-2017, 05:44 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3326-an-fhuiseog","name":"An Fhuiseog","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3326_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"271"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-22T08:36:12-07:00","id":1082274,"title":"","content":"But the geometric scale does not reflect reality. The geometric scale stops at 16 extra languages, when four times that number is a more realistic maximum.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-22T14:09:23-07:00","id":1082387,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>An Fhuiseog</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1081457-languages-a-background-or-a-knowledge?p=1082198#post1082198\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No there are studies with adults as well, I can give you references if you want.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm curious, though it seems to be getting rather off topic.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I meant absolutely in the sense of &quot;ignoring the relative&quot;, rather than &quot; absolute&quot; as in &quot;always true&quot;. </div> </div> </div>OK, however that doesn't really change anything, but lets go with the clarified statement instead:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Better expressed, the speed up in third language acquisition will not cause more distant languages to become easier than those in the same family. </div> </div> </div>That I can accept, however the issue remains that the speed up in question might be &quot;normal&quot; but it isn't universal. Not everyone is going to experience a speed up.<br /> <br /> As well, this is not reflected in any of the rules. While the XP &quot;bump&quot; between the first and second dot does mean that if you're buying languages with the Linguistics model and starting at Linguistics zero (and a character with a native language, characters that aren't born human do not always get the default free fluent language), that your third language is slightly cheaper than your second language, the scaling causes further languages to continually cost less:<br /> <br /> First language: free.<br /> Second language: 3 XP<br /> Third language: 2 XP<br /> Fourth and fifth: 2 XP per language<br /> Sixth through ninth language: 3/2 XP per language<br /> Tenth through seventeenth languages: 1 XP per language<br /> <br /> So the old model doesn't follow your own statements about the rate of acquisition where there's a plateau effect, as languages get cheaper and cheaper in XP value.<br /> <br /> Neither model is actually realistic, because XP isn't realistic to real learning in general.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> All major meta-studies demonstrate that languages with a historical or syntactic relationship to ones own are acquired faster. </div> </div> </div>Meta-studies are about confirming the results of individual studies for the key scientific goal of ensuring that results are repeatable. They show that despite any variation between individual studies, that they all support (or don't, as the case may be) a scientific consensus on the theory involved. A meta-study that shows a large amount of consistency in supporting individual hypotheses to support a broader theory doesn't mean anything to whether or not the results are universal. A meta-study just increases the confidence that the consensus result is the most accurate estimation of how prevalent the effect is.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I've never read an account of such a disability, how does it affect their acquisition of closer languages vs further ones? What do you mean by closer, other Indo-European languages? </div> </div> </div>As I already stated, my father and sister have trouble with muddled rules in systems that are too close to each other. For my sister, learning French after Spanish was extremely difficult (she literally failed her first French class which lead to her being officially diagnosed) because the commonalities between the two languages only obscured the differences. She aced Hebrew (which is a radically different language from English or Spanish) because it was easier for her to keep the rules separate. Language A follows rules A, language B follows rules B, and language C follows rules C. Learning the languages as discrete entities was easier for her than learning them as one building off the other; negating any speed up that would have happened.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1081457-languages-a-background-or-a-knowledge?p=1082274#post1082274\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But the geometric scale does not reflect reality. The geometric scale stops at 16 extra languages, when four times that number is a more realistic maximum.</div> </div> </div> </div>Technically, some of the versions of Natural Linguist also doubled the languages from Linguistics, so if you're using one of those, the max is 33, not 17. Still shy of how far humans can actually go, but it's easily enough to represent an extremely talented individual (esp. if you get a bit loose with what counts as a single language)<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-22T14:29:20-07:00","id":1082390,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nothing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1081457-languages-a-background-or-a-knowledge?p=1081739#post1081739\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is one of those times I throw out the rules and let players just take languages, if it makes sense for thier character. Anything more than a passing, casual conversational ability gets folded into Academics, and dead languages (or even Ecclesiastical Latin) falls under Academics at my table.<br /> <br /> Cheers!</div> </div> </div> </div>I had a similar take. <i>Multilingual</i> as a 1 point merit that lets you be conversant in whatever handful of languages suit your character's background, and <i>Master of Languages</i> (3 or 4 points, IIRC), that lets you use an Academics role to see if you understand any language, with difficulty depending on what language and how you might've been exposed to it. Said difficulty being slightly easier if one is playing in the sort of genre of Scion or Adventure!.<br /> <br /> (I had to come up with this originally for Eden's Buffy the Vampire Slayer RPG, whose language rules were as bad, if not worse, given that this was a setting in which Giles would pull what ever language fluency out of his English arse that was needed for the plot. &quot;It's a golly good thing that I happen to be perfectly fluent in this form of charades signs used by a tribe of one-armed Micronesian dwarves who died out 3000 years ago!&quot;)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-22T14:46:49-07:00","id":1082397,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1081457-languages-a-background-or-a-knowledge?p=1082387#post1082387\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As well, this is not reflected in any of the rules......<br /> Neither model is actually realistic, because XP isn't realistic to real learning in general.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ha!, yes indeed you are right here, I had gone so far off-topic that I'd forgotten this was a discussion of a system in the WoD! I was really only talking about real-life language acquisition.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1081457-languages-a-background-or-a-knowledge?p=1082387#post1082387\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Meta-studies are about confirming the results of individual studies for the key scientific goal of ensuring that results are repeatable. They show that despite any variation between individual studies, that they all support (or don't, as the case may be) a scientific consensus on the theory involved. A meta-study that shows a large amount of consistency in supporting individual hypotheses to support a broader theory doesn't mean anything to whether or not the results are universal. A meta-study just increases the confidence that the consensus result is the most accurate estimation of how prevalent the effect is.</div> </div> </div> </div>Of course, I'm unsure what you mean, but perhaps I was unclear.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1081457-languages-a-background-or-a-knowledge?p=1082387#post1082387\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As I already stated, my father and sister have trouble with muddled rules in systems that are too close to each other. For my sister, learning French after Spanish was extremely difficult (she literally failed her first French class which lead to her being officially diagnosed) because the commonalities between the two languages only obscured the differences. She aced Hebrew (which is a radically different language from English or Spanish) because it was easier for her to keep the rules separate. Language A follows rules A, language B follows rules B, and language C follows rules C. Learning the languages as discrete entities was easier for her than learning them as one building off the other; negating any speed up that would have happened.</div> </div> </div> </div>Closer languages been easier doesn't refer to French being easier after Spanish, but to both being easier due to their relationship with English, all else being equal. In this case French acquisition was affected by Spanish acquisition (this isn't uncommon in the population in general and is a noted effect), but that Spanish or French acquisition &quot;first-time round&quot; would be quicker than Hebrew acquisition &quot;first-time round&quot;.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1081457-languages-a-background-or-a-knowledge?p=1082387#post1082387\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That I can accept, however the issue remains that the speed up in question might be &quot;normal&quot; but it isn't universal. Not everyone is going to experience a speed up.</div> </div> </div> </div>They essentially have to, unless they didn't correctly acquire language acquisition skills from their L2.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3326-an-fhuiseog","name":"An Fhuiseog","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3326_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"271"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-22T16:02:07-07:00","id":1082418,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1081457-languages-a-background-or-a-knowledge?p=1082390#post1082390\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...and <i>Master of Languages</i> (3 or 4 points, IIRC), that lets you use an Academics role to see if you understand any language, with difficulty depending on what language and how you might've been exposed to it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd personally find it very unfun to have to buy a Merit just for the chance to roll to translate a language you aren't fluent in. This would only have value to me if it was something like being able to do so without time and/or resources for translation.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> (I had to come up with this originally for Eden's Buffy the Vampire Slayer RPG, whose language rules were as bad, if not worse, given that this was a setting in which Giles would pull what ever language fluency out of his English arse that was needed for the plot. &quot;It's a golly good thing that I happen to be perfectly fluent in this form of charades signs used by a tribe of one-armed Micronesian dwarves who died out 3000 years ago!&quot;) </div> </div> </div>There's a reason why a lot of games that aim to reproduce a specific show/movie/etc. have moved to more narrative focused mechanics. Giles is a lot easier to do in something like Fate where you just tag his &quot;Librarian of the Strange and the Occult,&quot; Aspect to have him just happen to know some obscure thing like this, than he is in the WoD system. They're just different systems aiming to focus on different results.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>An Fhuiseog</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1081457-languages-a-background-or-a-knowledge?p=1082397#post1082397\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Closer languages been easier doesn't refer to French being easier after Spanish, but to both being easier due to their relationship with English, all else being equal. In this case French acquisition was affected by Spanish acquisition (this isn't uncommon in the population in general and is a noted effect), but that Spanish or French acquisition &quot;first-time round&quot; would be quicker than Hebrew acquisition &quot;first-time round&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>This doesn't jive with both this:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> They essentially have to, unless they didn't correctly acquire language acquisition skills from their L2. </div> </div> </div>And this:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It is known to be the case experimentally that third language acquisition is faster than second. The &quot;speed up&quot; is mostly &quot;language distance&quot; invariant, although languages closer to one's own are always easier absolutely. </div> </div> </div>You've said that learning a third language is always faster than the second, the speed up is distance invariant, closer languages make things easier, second language can negative impact third language learning, and that closer only matters to first language.<br /> <br /> These cannot all be true.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-22T16:42:13-07:00","id":1082432,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1081457-languages-a-background-or-a-knowledge?p=1082418#post1082418\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You've said that learning a third language is always faster than the second, the speed up is distance invariant, closer languages make things easier, second language can negative impact third language learning, and that closer only matters to first language.<br /> <br /> These cannot all be true.</div> </div> </div> </div>Of course they can, which two contradict?<br /> <br /> Restating, what linguistics says is:<br /> <br /> (a) Acquisition of an L2 imparts skills than can be used for L(n) acquisition, improving the rate of that acquisition. The improvement does not seem to vary across syntactic or historical relationships, i.e. there is a &quot;constant&quot; improvement, coming from acquiring language acquisition skills.<br /> (b) Acquisition of L(n)s are affected by the historical relationship of that L(n) with one's own L1.<br /> (c) There is an observed &quot;confusion&quot; effect when learning similar languages for some people. However studies do not show this &quot;overcoming&quot; (a).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3326-an-fhuiseog","name":"An Fhuiseog","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3326_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"271"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-22T17:32:48-07:00","id":1082451,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1081457-languages-a-background-or-a-knowledge?p=1082194#post1082194\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No, it isn't. The key word is &quot;absolutely,&quot; because that is saying that something is 100% true in all cases is incorrect if presented with contrary evidence; even if considered outliers.<br /> <br /> As well, we only call them learning disabilities because it slots them into legislation to protect the education of children with disabilities to ensure appropriate steps are taken. All a learning disability is, is when &quot;normal&quot; teaching methods don't work for a student severely enough that a certified professional signs off of them needing alternate methods of instruction.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That there are outliers doesn't mean there isn't an average. That you can pull out people who learn differently doesn't change that there seems to be some evidence that multiple languages make it easier OR at least its no less realistic than weapons damage..<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> [quote}This doesn't make any sense as a defense of the geometric Linguistics Knowledge model of pre-20th.<br /> <br /> An Ability dot is worth 2 freebies. The value of Linguistics doesn't get cheaper than the Language Merit until Linguistics 5 (at which point you're dealing with 16 languages, and are certainly in the point of making it hard to make them all matter to the plot). The &quot;linear&quot; Merit approach is better because individual languages are cheap until you get into the very high numbers of them. You can get the 1-2 extra languages that you feel are worth taking for player for less investment than using the old version.<br /> <br /> [/QUOTE]<br /> <br /> I also use Flat xp/Cwod 2e xp rather than classic system I think a linear progreassion of the merit works better but level should be 3 additional and so on and so forth","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-23T12:14:31-07:00","id":1082730,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1081457-languages-a-background-or-a-knowledge?p=1082418#post1082418\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'd personally find it very unfun to have to buy a Merit just for the chance to roll to translate a language you aren't fluent in. This would only have value to me if it was something like being able to do so without time and/or resources for translation.</div> </div> </div> </div>That was generally the intent, yes. You roll Academics, Socialize or whatever ability is suitable for the &quot;Oh, I understand this&quot; effect when some NPC starts speaking Mandarin or you come across some tablet engraved with Biblical era Hebrew. I never used it as a &quot;you sit in a library for six hours with several books on Byzantine Greek&quot; situation. That's just an extended Academics role anyone can make. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-23T13:07:38-07:00","id":1082747,"title":"","content":"But that is a rather absurd position, at least in the US. I took four years of High School French, one semester of undergraduate French, one semester of undergraduate German, and three semesters of undergraduate Portuguese, but I doubt that I could speak any of those three languages, and I have four degrees. The majority of former US students are just incapable of speaking the foreign languages that they learned in high school or during their undergraduate studies unless they actually majored in the language (or spent a few years studying in a country where the language was spoken).<br /> <br /> You could make an argument that Academics could be used to puzzle out texts from a familiar language, though it would take ten times as much time as if your character actually knew the language in question (and it would really have to be something that would be covered by Academics, such as dead languages like Ancient Greek, Ancient Hebrew, Babylonian, Classical Latin, Classical Mandarin, Sumerian, etc). The Merit represents fluency in the language while Academics would represent a familiarity with the literature of the languages that your character knows. I would not allow Socialize to substitute for any language though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-23T15:34:20-07:00","id":1082792,"title":"","content":"I'm very much insistent on using the Knowledge and think the merit is rather absurd. Namely due to the fact that you gain more and more languages per point taken is far more reflective of the truth: languages get easier to learn the more you know. Secondly, the option of having a skill to roll to figure out some old text or messed up transmission in German is way more practical for me. Having it under Academics is overloading an already overloaded ability, which contains philosophy, psychology, anthropology, and sociology. There's already an ability for Computers and Technology, and one separate for Science, yet the humanities are all shoved into one.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1VN49Y7tH2ZV0l7Hx65RWX1ez-Q9Lst-8ZTyTJeCTpxM/\" target=\"_blank\">Sorcerer 20th</a> homebrew and my update to <a href=\"http://immortalthegathering.blogspot.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Highlander: the Gathering</a> for 20th Anniversary edition.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2414-theoutlander523","name":"theoutlander523","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2414_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"238"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-23T16:33:23-07:00","id":1082818,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>theoutlander523</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1081457-languages-a-background-or-a-knowledge?p=1082792#post1082792\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm very much insistent on using the Knowledge and think the merit is rather absurd. Namely due to the fact that you gain more and more languages per point taken is far more reflective of the truth: languages get easier to learn the more you know.</div> </div> </div> </div>M20 introduced a function where if you put 5+ points into the Language merit, you can make an Intelligence + Engimas roll to try your hand at understanding unfamiliar languages. Alternately, you could just give it the same escalation with each point you put into it. It's not really difficult to manage.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Secondly, the option of having a skill to roll to figure out some old text or messed up transmission in German is way more practical for me. Having it under Academics is overloading an already overloaded ability, which contains philosophy, psychology, anthropology, and sociology. There's already an ability for Computers and Technology, and one separate for Science, yet the humanities are all shoved into one. </div> </div> </div>The separation of Computers and Technology might not be the best example, since it's a very 90s design thing to do. You can probably piece out botched translations, provided that you know the language, with Enigmas or Investigation. Especially since Enigmas isn't usually doing much to begin with, as the &quot;like Investigation and Intelligence, but not really!&quot; Ability.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-23T17:56:40-07:00","id":1082855,"title":"","content":"I've gotta a lot of mileage out of Enigmas, as I tend to roll it to piece things together that I'm missing or to use it for logic problems. Also VtM doesn't have enigmas unfortunately, which kinda puts a small problem in that plan.<br /> <br /> As for computers, I always saw it as a measure of your ability to actually program and hack computers, not your ability to Google. Same with the drive skill, 90% of everyone should have one point in Drive and Computers if they didn't function like that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1VN49Y7tH2ZV0l7Hx65RWX1ez-Q9Lst-8ZTyTJeCTpxM/\" target=\"_blank\">Sorcerer 20th</a> homebrew and my update to <a href=\"http://immortalthegathering.blogspot.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Highlander: the Gathering</a> for 20th Anniversary edition.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2414-theoutlander523","name":"theoutlander523","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2414_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"238"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-23T20:36:30-07:00","id":1082884,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>theoutlander523</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1081457-languages-a-background-or-a-knowledge?p=1082855#post1082855\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've gotta a lot of mileage out of Enigmas, as I tend to roll it to piece things together that I'm missing or to use it for logic problems. Also VtM doesn't have enigmas unfortunately, which kinda puts a small problem in that plan.</div> </div> </div> </div>Again, not exactly a substantial barrier, that, since plenty of other games do have said Ability, so if you own even one of them, no issue at all.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> As for computers, I always saw it as a measure of your ability to actually program and hack computers, not your ability to Google. </div> </div> </div>Your Ability to use google is actually in Investigation, provided that you know how the interface and search engine work. Working with Electronics is Technology, and, well, computers are a form of electronics, so, yeah. Besides, we don't need a division of hardware and software like Shadowrun has. That's for games that want to divide everything up into tiny bits and then charge you out the nose for Skill Groups.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Same with the drive skill, 90% of everyone should have one point in Drive and Computers if they didn't function like that. </div> </div> </div>Even in modern society, you can arguably operate without a dot in either, since having an Ability covers actual technical knowledge and professional skill, and most people don't have a whole lot of either, even if they live with these devices and machines day-in, day-out. Lacking even familiarity is something different, which would probably constitute a flaw, like being Illiterate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-24T05:47:38-07:00","id":1082981,"title":"","content":"While I agree that most adults have Drive 1, the majority of people can no more program a computer than they can rebuild an engine, so Computer 1 is as uncommon as Technology 1. Using a computer is easy after a few weeks of exposure, the vast majority have very simple interfaces, but the vast majority of users would give up if they faced a DOS prompt.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}